  "question": {
    "text": "An ideal mixture of two liquids A and B is put in a cylinder containing piston. Piston is pulled out isothermally so that the volume of liquid decreases but that of vapours increases. Negligibly small amount of liquid was left and mole-fraction of A in vapour is 0.4. If&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>P</mtext> <mtext>A</mtext> <mo>∘</mo> </msubsup> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>0.4</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <msubsup> <mtext>P</mtext> <mtext>B</mtext> <mo>∘</mo> </msubsup> <mo>=</mo> <mtext>1.2</mtext> </mrow> </math>&nbsp;atm at the experimental temperature, which of the following is the total pressure at which the liquid is almost evaporated?",
    "image": null
  },
